e, and the complement of the complement is the graph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"made simple and loop-free. O(1); a lazy view.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/inducedSubgraphView(on:)-3ckvb":{"abstract":[{"text":"The subgraph induced by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":": those vertices and every edge between them, as a lazy","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"view (igraph’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"induced_subgraph"},{"text":", NetworkX’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"G.subgraph(nodes)"},{"text":"). The kept vertices are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"numbered in the graph’s order, whatever the listed order; a vertex listed twice is kept","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"once. The view keeps the graph’s edge positions and has no edge indices.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"inducedSubgraphView(on:)","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/inducedSubgraphView(on:)-3ckvb","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/inducedsubgraphview(on:)-3ckvb","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"inducedSubgraphView"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"on"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ST","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Sequence"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">) -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:15GraphOperations12SubgraphViewV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SubgraphView"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentif